Silk (est.) embroidery on unidentified ground fiber border: needle lace, burato (twined ground and darned in one direction)', 'assets/patterns/archive-CMA-103790.webp', 'assets/patterns/archive-CMA-103790-thumb.webp', '7a0ea813d4b51b8bbc352b2f0d2bc0d4cf9718e4566edf00acc6bf88ff41eee5', NULL, 3400, 2867, '克利夫兰艺术博物馆', '克利夫兰艺术博物馆', 'https://clevelandart.org/art/1921.84', NULL, '馆方未注明', 'CC0', 'https://www.clevelandart.org/open-access', '1921.84', NULL, NULL, 'Notable for its bright and valued colors, this cover has a needle lace border of natural and organic motifs attached to a silk cloth. The lace is divided into two registers, possibly representing stylized plants and flowers growing above ground with their roots growing in pots beneath them.', NULL, '中文检索名与题材标签由本素材库整理；原作名称及文化归属以馆方原文为准。', FALSE, 0, '花卉 · 边饰 欧洲与其他传统  花草藤蔓 边饰与织锦');

